course: dictionary
lesson: 12553
title: Developed: grown and changed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Developed» is the past form of «develop». When something develops, it grows, changes or improves over time. «The tadpole developed legs over the summer.» The tadpole did not get legs in one moment. It changed bit by bit until it had them.
explain: Developed can also be an adjective, a describing word. «Ava wrote a well-developed story with a brave hero and a surprising ending.» Well-developed means full of detail and carefully built up, not thin or rushed.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Many people live in developed countries, where there are lots of factories, shops and services.» Here developed describes a country that has grown rich with many industries, so the clues tell you what it means.
fact: Develop means to grow, change, make or improve over time.
fact: «Developed» means grown, advanced or fully formed.
fact: «A well-developed plan» has been thought through with lots of detail.
fact: A developed country is a rich country with many industries and services.
fact: «Developed into» means changed slowly into something new, as in «The idea developed into a club».
exercise: «The tadpole developed legs over the summer.» What does developed mean here? | *Grew and changed over time | Swam away from the pond | Stayed exactly the same | Lost its tail in one second
exercise: «Her story was well-developed, full of detail.» What does well-developed mean? | Finished last week | Written in pencil | *Full of detail and carefully built up | Very short and rushed
exercise: Maya reads, «Many people live in developed countries.» What is a developed country? | *A rich country with many industries and services | A small village with one shop | A country under the sea | A country with no roads
test: «The small idea developed into a huge school project.» What does developed into mean? | Stopped completely | *Changed slowly over time into something new | Broke into little pieces | Was thrown away
test: Which word is the past form of develop? | Developing | Developer | Develops | *Developed
exam: «The newly developed park has a pond, paths and benches.» What does newly developed suggest? | Covered in snow all year | *Recently made or improved | Very old and falling apart | Closed forever
